IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 77 (options over unissued shares) and s 78 (power of a company to pay interest out of capital in certain cases).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 9244-9298 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Section 77: options over unissued shares`

-- The two dates the section names. "granted after 29 December 1967" is the keel's constant; "granted on or after 18 November 1998" is this section's.
`s 77(1A) the day 18 November 1998` MEANS Date 18 11 1998

-- (2): subsections (1) and (1A) "do not apply in any case where the holders of debentures have an option to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures".
-- src:9259 | (2) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply in any case where the
-- src:9260 | holders of debentures have an option to take up shares of the company
-- src:9261 | by way of redemption of the debentures.
@ref s 77(2) (src:9259-9261)
GIVEN `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(2) subsection (1) or (1A) applies to the option` MEANS
    IF `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply in any case where the holders of debentures have an option to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says when (1) and (1A) do not apply; it does not say when they do

-- (1): a public company's option granted after 29 December 1967 that enables any person to take up unissued shares after 5 years have elapsed from the grant is void.
-- "after a period of 5 years has elapsed from the date on which the option was granted": the option can be exercised on a day later than the last day of the 5 years (the keel's P1 and P4). Taken: an option exercisable at any time after the 5 years is caught (fork F-S1).
-- src:9246 | 77.—(1) An option granted after 29 December 1967 by a public
-- src:9247 | company which enables any person to take up unissued shares of the
-- src:9248 | company after a period of 5 years has elapsed from the date on which
-- src:9249 | the option was granted is void.
@ref s 77(1) (src:9246-9249)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the option was granted` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the option enables a person to take up unissued shares of the company` IS A DATE
      `the option enables an employee of the company or of its related corporation (including any director holding a salaried office or employment in that company or corporation) to take up unissued shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1) the option is void under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply in any case where the holders of debentures have an option to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures" (section 77(2), a flat negative) {F-S2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR `the date the option was granted` AT MOST `the day 29 December 1967`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An option granted after 29 December 1967 by a public company"; an option of a private company, or granted on or before that day, is outside it {MR-b}
          ELSE (IF `the option enables an employee of the company or of its related corporation (including any director holding a salaried office or employment in that company or corporation) to take up unissued shares of the company` AND `the date the option was granted` AT LEAST `s 77(1A) the day 18 November 1998`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (1) does not apply to such an option" (section 77(1A); "such an option" read as an employee's option granted on or after 18 November 1998, fork F-S3) {F-S3} {MR-a}
                ELSE (IF `the last day on which the option enables a person to take up unissued shares of the company` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the option was granted` 5 Years
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which enables any person to take up unissued shares of the company after a period of 5 years has elapsed from the date on which the option was granted is void" -- an option that cannot be taken up after the 5 years is not described by the subsection (a period the text fixes in its own words, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)) {F-S1} {MR-a}

-- src:9251 | (1A) An option granted on or after 18 November 1998 by a public
-- src:9252 | company which enables any employee of that company or its related
-- src:9253 | corporation (including any director holding a salaried office or
-- src:9254 | employment in that company or corporation) to take up unissued
-- src:9255 | shares of the company after a period of 10 years has elapsed from the
-- src:9256 | date on which the option was granted is void and subsection (1) does
-- src:9257 | not apply to such an option.
@ref s 77(1A) (src:9251-9257)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the option was granted` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the option enables a person to take up unissued shares of the company` IS A DATE
      `the option enables an employee of the company or of its related corporation (including any director holding a salaried office or employment in that company or corporation) to take up unissued shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1A) the option is void under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF `the option is an option of the holders of debentures to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply in any case where the holders of debentures have an option to take up shares of the company by way of redemption of the debentures" (section 77(2), a flat negative) {F-S2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    (NOT `the company is a public company`)
             OR (NOT `the option enables an employee of the company or of its related corporation (including any director holding a salaried office or employment in that company or corporation) to take up unissued shares of the company`)
             OR `the date the option was granted` LESS THAN `s 77(1A) the day 18 November 1998`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An option granted on or after 18 November 1998 by a public company which enables any employee of that company or its related corporation ... to take up unissued shares"; any other option is outside it {MR-b}
          ELSE (IF `the last day on which the option enables a person to take up unissued shares of the company` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the option was granted` 10 Years
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to take up unissued shares of the company after a period of 10 years has elapsed from the date on which the option was granted is void" -- an option that cannot be taken up after the 10 years is not described by the subsection (a period the text fixes in its own words, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)) {F-S1} {MR-a}

§ `Section 78: power of a company to pay interest out of capital in certain cases`

-- The opening words: "Where any shares of a company are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period, the company may pay interest on so much of such share capital (except treasury shares) as is for the time being paid up".
-- src:9265 | 78. Where any shares of a company are issued for the purpose of
-- src:9266 | raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works
-- src:9267 | or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made
-- src:9268 | profitable for a long period, the company may pay interest on so much
-- src:9269 | of such share capital (except treasury shares) as is for the time being
-- src:9270 | paid up and charge the interest so paid to capital as part of the cost of
-- src:9271 | the construction or provision but —
@ref s 78 (src:9265-9271)
GIVEN `the shares are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the share capital that is for the time being paid up` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of that paid-up share capital that is held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78 the amount of share capital on which the company may pay interest` MEANS
    IF `the shares are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period`
    THEN JUST (`the amount of the share capital that is for the time being paid up` MINUS `the amount of that paid-up share capital that is held as treasury shares`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any shares of a company are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period"; shares issued for another purpose are outside it {MR-b}

-- (a): "no such payment may be made unless it is authorised, by the constitution or by special resolution, and is approved by the Court". A bar: TRUE where the payment is barred.
-- src:9273 | (a) no such payment may be made unless it is authorised, by
-- src:9274 | the constitution or by special resolution, and is approved
-- src:9275 | by the Court;
@ref s 78(a) (src:9273-9275)
GIVEN `the payment is authorised by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is authorised by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is approved by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(a) the payment of interest out of capital is barred` MEANS
    IF (`the payment is authorised by the constitution` OR `the payment is authorised by special resolution`) AND `the payment is approved by the Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no such payment may be made unless it is authorised, by the constitution or by special resolution, and is approved by the Court" -- the "unless" is met {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (b): before approving, the Court may at the company's expense appoint a person to inquire and report, and may require the company to give security for the costs of the inquiry.
-- src:9280 | (b) before approving any such payment, the Court may at the
-- src:9281 | expense of the company appoint a person to inquire and
-- src:9282 | report as to the circumstances of the case, and may require
-- src:9283 | the company to give security for the payment of the costs
-- src:9284 | of the inquiry;
@ref s 78(b) (src:9280-9284)
GIVEN `the Court has appointed a person to inquire and report as to the circumstances of the case before approving the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(b) the expense of the inquiry falls on the company` MEANS
    IF `the Court has appointed a person to inquire and report as to the circumstances of the case before approving the payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before approving any such payment, the Court may at the expense of the company appoint a person to inquire and report"; with no appointment there is no expense to bear {MR-b}

-- src:9280 | (b) before approving any such payment, the Court may at the
-- src:9281 | expense of the company appoint a person to inquire and
-- src:9282 | report as to the circumstances of the case, and may require
-- src:9283 | the company to give security for the payment of the costs
-- src:9284 | of the inquiry;
@ref s 78(b) (src:9280-9284)
GIVEN `the Court has appointed a person to inquire and report as to the circumstances of the case before approving the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has already approved the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(b) the company may be required to give security for the costs of the inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the Court has appointed a person to inquire and report as to the circumstances of the case before approving the payment` AND (NOT `the Court has already approved the payment`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court "may require the company to give security for the payment of the costs of the inquiry" before approving; without an inquiry, or after approval, the text gives no such power {MR-b}

-- (c): "the payment is to be made only for such period as is determined by the Court, but in no case extending beyond a period of 12 months after the works or buildings have been actually completed or the plant provided".
-- src:9286 | (c) the payment is to be made only for such period as is
-- src:9287 | determined by the Court, but in no case extending beyond a
-- src:9288 | period of 12 months after the works or buildings have been
-- src:9289 | actually completed or the plant provided;
@ref s 78(c) (src:9286-9289)
GIVEN `the last day of the period the Court has determined` IS A DATE
      `the day the works or buildings have been actually completed or the plant provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78(c) the last day to which the payment may be made` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period the Court has determined` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the works or buildings have been actually completed or the plant provided` 12 Months
    THEN `the last day of the period the Court has determined`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the works or buildings have been actually completed or the plant provided` 12 Months

-- (d): "the rate of interest must in no case exceed 5% per annum or such other rate as is for the time being prescribed". A bar: TRUE where the rate is above the limit.
-- src:9291 | (d) the rate of interest must in no case exceed 5% per annum or
-- src:9292 | such other rate as is for the time being prescribed; and
@ref s 78(d) (src:9291-9292)
GIVEN `the rate of interest, in per cent per annum` IS A NUMBER
      `another rate is for the time being prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate for the time being prescribed, in per cent per annum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(d) the rate of interest exceeds the limit` MEANS
    IF `the rate of interest, in per cent per annum` GREATER THAN (IF `another rate is for the time being prescribed` THEN `the rate for the time being prescribed, in per cent per annum` ELSE 5)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the rate of interest must in no case exceed 5% per annum or such other rate as is for the time being prescribed" (a flat negative; a rate within the limit is not barred by this paragraph) {MR-a}

-- src:9294 | (e) the payment of the interest does not operate as a reduction
-- src:9295 | of the amount paid up on the shares in respect of which it is
-- src:9296 | paid.
@ref s 78(e) (src:9294-9296)
GIVEN `the interest is paid under section 78` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(e) the payment of the interest operates as a reduction of the amount paid up on the shares in respect of which it is paid` MEANS
    IF `the interest is paid under section 78`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the payment of the interest does not operate as a reduction of the amount paid up on the shares in respect of which it is paid" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the payment of the interest under section 78; another payment is outside it {MR-b}

-- The whole section: the company may pay the interest and charge it to capital as part of the cost, "but" within (a) to (e).
-- src:9265 | 78. Where any shares of a company are issued for the purpose of
-- src:9266 | raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works
-- src:9267 | or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made
-- src:9268 | profitable for a long period, the company may pay interest on so much
-- src:9269 | of such share capital (except treasury shares) as is for the time being
-- src:9270 | paid up and charge the interest so paid to capital as part of the cost of
-- src:9271 | the construction or provision but —
-- src:9273 | (a) no such payment may be made unless it is authorised, by
-- src:9274 | the constitution or by special resolution, and is approved
-- src:9275 | by the Court;
-- src:9280 | (b) before approving any such payment, the Court may at the
-- src:9281 | expense of the company appoint a person to inquire and
-- src:9282 | report as to the circumstances of the case, and may require
-- src:9283 | the company to give security for the payment of the costs
-- src:9284 | of the inquiry;
-- src:9286 | (c) the payment is to be made only for such period as is
-- src:9287 | determined by the Court, but in no case extending beyond a
-- src:9288 | period of 12 months after the works or buildings have been
-- src:9289 | actually completed or the plant provided;
-- src:9291 | (d) the rate of interest must in no case exceed 5% per annum or
-- src:9292 | such other rate as is for the time being prescribed; and
-- src:9294 | (e) the payment of the interest does not operate as a reduction
-- src:9295 | of the amount paid up on the shares in respect of which it is
-- src:9296 | paid.
@ref s 78 (src:9265-9296)
GIVEN `the shares are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is authorised by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is authorised by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is approved by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate of interest, in per cent per annum` IS A NUMBER
      `another rate is for the time being prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate for the time being prescribed, in per cent per annum` IS A NUMBER
      `the payment is made for a period ending no later than the last day to which the payment may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78 the company may pay interest on the paid-up share capital and charge it to capital as part of the cost` MEANS
    IF    `the shares are issued for the purpose of raising money to defray the expenses of the construction of any works or buildings or the provision of any plant which cannot be made profitable for a long period`
      AND `s 78(a) the payment of interest out of capital is barred` `the payment is authorised by the constitution` `the payment is authorised by special resolution` `the payment is approved by the Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
      AND `s 78(d) the rate of interest exceeds the limit` `the rate of interest, in per cent per annum` `another rate is for the time being prescribed` `the rate for the time being prescribed, in per cent per annum` EQUALS JUST FALSE
      AND `the payment is made for a period ending no later than the last day to which the payment may be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the company may pay interest ... but — (a) no such payment may be made unless ...; (c) the payment is to be made only for such period ...; (d) the rate of interest must in no case exceed ...") whose limits are not all met; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (each limit has its own function, which says no in the text's words) {F-S4} {MR-b}
